      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx} + \\frac{1}{y^{2}} = 1.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(x)=c$. Set $dy/dx=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nFirst keep the original domain: $y\\ne0$.\n\nRearranging once, test whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\nf(c) = 1 - \\frac{1}{c^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For $c=-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) &=-1 + 1 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) &=-1 + 1 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) &=- \\frac{1}{4} + 1 \\\\ &=\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=-1$ and $y=1$.",
